==English==

===Etymology===
From {{w|Samuel Plimsoll}}, Bristol merchant and member of Parliament; promoter of the ''Merchant Shipping Act''.

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|nautical}} Properly the [[International Load Line]], a mark on the [[hull]] of a [[merchant ship]] to show the [[waterline]] under specified conditions. The line shows the maximum capacity load the ship may carry.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|load line}}
* {{l|en|load water line}}
* {{l|en|Plimsoll mark}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|plimsoll}}

